title: Synthetic Monitoring: Worker Scheduler
agents: linux
catalog: app/synmon
license: MIT
distribution: check_mk
description:
 One service per synthetic-monitoring worker host, sourced from the
 {synmon_worker} agent section (the executor's heartbeat plus an agent-side
 spool scan). Goes WARN/CRIT when the scheduler heartbeat is too old (the
 executor stalled), CRIT when the last run failed as a whole (e.g. the browser
 did not start; the error is shown), and WARN when unparseable spool files
 are present or journey files failed to load (invalid target host, or a
 name/id that collides with another journey on the same host). It is also
 WARN when results for target hosts outside the worker's allowlist
 (/etc/synmon/allowed_hosts) were dropped, when the agent plugin's read
 limit (500 files / 16 MiB) was reached, or when the worker has no allowlist.
 Perfdata: heartbeat age, results found, journeys failed, unparseable count.

 Configure heartbeat-age thresholds with the ruleset
 "Synthetic monitoring: worker scheduler".
